1
00:00:27,694 --> 00:00:29,696
[♪♪♪]

3
00:02:37,449 --> 00:02:39,034
[Boy speaks indistinctly]

4
00:02:41,244 --> 00:02:43,205
Boy: Ha! Ha!

5
00:02:43,372 --> 00:02:44,539
[Speaks in foreign language]

6
00:02:45,957 --> 00:02:47,959
[Yelling indistinctly]

7
00:02:51,630 --> 00:02:53,548
Come, come!

8
00:02:57,844 --> 00:02:59,304
Please! Please! Please!

9
00:03:01,556 --> 00:03:03,558
[♪♪♪]

10
00:03:14,111 --> 00:03:17,280
[Whispering] Aziz. Aziz.

11
00:03:20,367 --> 00:03:22,494
Aziz, light!

12
00:03:22,994 --> 00:03:24,204
Aziz, light.

13
00:03:28,917 --> 00:03:30,460
We start again.

14
00:03:31,878 --> 00:03:36,258
"When the three planets are in eclipse,
the black hole, like a door, is opened.

15
00:03:36,425 --> 00:03:38,176
Evil comes...

16
00:03:38,343 --> 00:03:40,762
Spreading terror and chaos."

17
00:03:40,929 --> 00:03:44,349
See the snake, Billy? The ultimate evil.

18
00:03:44,516 --> 00:03:47,477
- Make sure you get the snake.
- Yes, I've got your snakes.

19
00:03:47,644 --> 00:03:49,146
I got all the snakes.

20
00:03:49,312 --> 00:03:51,565
So when is this snake act
supposed to occur?

21
00:03:51,732 --> 00:03:55,152
Huh? Well, if this is the five...

22
00:03:55,318 --> 00:03:57,446
And this is the one...

23
00:03:57,779 --> 00:03:59,781
[Whispering indistinctly]

24
00:04:02,325 --> 00:04:03,910
Every 5000 years.

25
00:04:04,995 --> 00:04:07,914
So I've got some time, then.

26
00:04:08,081 --> 00:04:09,666
[Snoring]

27
00:04:13,670 --> 00:04:15,297
[Gasps]

28
00:04:15,464 --> 00:04:17,632
Ah, you bring them water.

29
00:04:18,008 --> 00:04:20,177
Good boy. I will take it to them.

30
00:04:20,343 --> 00:04:22,637
Go with god. Be safe from evil.

31
00:04:24,347 --> 00:04:28,059
Pacoli: You see here these
different peoples, or symbols of people...

32
00:04:28,226 --> 00:04:33,398
Gathering together the four elements
of life: Water, fire, earth, air...

33
00:04:33,565 --> 00:04:35,275
Around a fifth one.

34
00:04:35,442 --> 00:04:36,985
A fifth...

35
00:04:37,819 --> 00:04:38,862
Element.

36
00:04:42,532 --> 00:04:44,201
Forgive me, lord.

37
00:04:44,367 --> 00:04:46,328
They already know too much.

38
00:04:48,413 --> 00:04:50,040
[Glass clinks]

39
00:04:50,791 --> 00:04:52,042
Ah, father.

40
00:04:52,501 --> 00:04:55,212
- Yes, how are you today?
- Well, Billy. You have some glasses?

41
00:04:55,378 --> 00:04:57,547
- Of course.
- Father, I'm so glad to see you.

42
00:04:57,714 --> 00:04:59,174
It's the most extraordinary thing.

43
00:04:59,341 --> 00:05:01,718
I mean, look,
it's the greatest find in history.

44
00:05:01,885 --> 00:05:04,054
Yes. You must be parched.

45
00:05:04,221 --> 00:05:07,057
Huh? Oh, yes, yes. I'm sorry.

46
00:05:09,768 --> 00:05:11,603
I mean, it's like a battle plan.

47
00:05:11,770 --> 00:05:14,731
Here, the good. Here, the evil.

48
00:05:15,065 --> 00:05:19,402
And here, a weapon against evil.

49
00:05:21,071 --> 00:05:23,073
I'm going to be famous.

50
00:05:23,240 --> 00:05:26,326
Then... then let us...
Let us toast to your fame.

51
00:05:26,493 --> 00:05:28,870
Oh, yes. To fame.

52
00:05:29,454 --> 00:05:30,622
Salute.

53
00:05:34,668 --> 00:05:38,046
You can't drink a toast with water.
Billy, in my sack, the grappa.

54
00:05:40,048 --> 00:05:42,050
[Men yelling nearby]

55
00:05:44,135 --> 00:05:46,137
[♪♪♪]

56
00:05:47,556 --> 00:05:49,432
[Groans]

57
00:05:50,725 --> 00:05:52,477
This I don't understand. But this...

58
00:05:52,644 --> 00:05:54,437
This could be something...

59
00:05:54,604 --> 00:05:56,273
Prehistoric.

60
00:05:56,439 --> 00:05:57,732
Maybe. I don't know.

61
00:05:59,067 --> 00:06:00,944
But wait.

62
00:06:01,444 --> 00:06:03,488
Here. Here.

63
00:06:04,531 --> 00:06:06,533
[Children laughing nearby]

64
00:06:10,745 --> 00:06:12,163
Boy: Look, look.

65
00:06:22,924 --> 00:06:24,551
They're here.

66
00:06:29,639 --> 00:06:32,017
Pacoli: This man...

67
00:06:32,183 --> 00:06:34,269
This perfect being.

68
00:06:34,769 --> 00:06:36,813
I know this is the key. I know it.

69
00:06:43,194 --> 00:06:45,322
This divine light they talk about.

70
00:06:45,488 --> 00:06:47,490
What is divine light?

71
00:06:48,950 --> 00:06:50,118
Aziz, light!

72
00:06:52,162 --> 00:06:54,039
Much better. Thank you, Aziz.

73
00:07:10,805 --> 00:07:12,349
My lord.

74
00:07:33,828 --> 00:07:35,830
[Mouthing]

75
00:07:44,381 --> 00:07:46,383
[Growling]

76
00:07:54,557 --> 00:07:58,520
Father, this is the most unbelievable thing
I have ever seen.

77
00:07:58,687 --> 00:07:59,771
Don't you think...?

78
00:08:02,774 --> 00:08:04,484
[Stammering]

79
00:08:04,651 --> 00:08:06,736
Are you German?

80
00:08:09,781 --> 00:08:13,076
Lord, I know he was about
to discover everything.

81
00:08:13,243 --> 00:08:16,287
But there is no worry.
I was there in time.

82
00:08:16,663 --> 00:08:19,582
Mondoshawan:
Priest, you and those before you...

83
00:08:19,749 --> 00:08:22,127
Have served us well.

84
00:08:22,293 --> 00:08:24,129
But war is coming.

85
00:08:24,295 --> 00:08:28,341
Stones not safe on earth anymore.

86
00:08:46,609 --> 00:08:48,319
Is really amazing.

87
00:09:00,248 --> 00:09:02,250
[Growling and snorting]

88
00:09:10,842 --> 00:09:12,844
[♪♪♪]

89
00:09:19,726 --> 00:09:21,561
The fifth element.

90
00:09:23,521 --> 00:09:25,482
Take the stones.

91
00:10:05,855 --> 00:10:07,232
My lord...

92
00:10:07,398 --> 00:10:11,027
If you take the weapon, we will be
defenseless when evil returns.

93
00:10:11,194 --> 00:10:15,949
In 300 years, when evil returns...

94
00:10:16,116 --> 00:10:18,034
So shall we.

95
00:10:25,917 --> 00:10:27,460
Oh, professor.

96
00:10:28,002 --> 00:10:29,129
Professor.

97
00:10:33,716 --> 00:10:35,718
[Stammering]

98
00:10:35,885 --> 00:10:37,095
Don't move!

99
00:10:38,888 --> 00:10:40,390
-I have a gun! Priest: Billy.

100
00:10:40,557 --> 00:10:44,018
Please, understand. They are our friends.

101
00:10:44,185 --> 00:10:45,395
Fflends?

102
00:10:45,562 --> 00:10:48,982
Father, they've killed the professor!
They're monsters!

103
00:10:49,149 --> 00:10:51,067
I'll explain everything. Billy.

104
00:10:51,568 --> 00:10:53,361
- You're with them?
- Billy, look at me.

105
00:10:53,528 --> 00:10:54,779
Look at me. I am your friend.

106
00:10:54,946 --> 00:10:57,365
- No, father.
- Billy, look at me!

107
00:10:57,532 --> 00:11:01,619
Please, put the gun down.

108
00:11:03,413 --> 00:11:04,873
Billy, no!

109
00:11:05,039 --> 00:11:06,291
[Mon doshawan groans]

110
00:11:06,457 --> 00:11:08,001
[Rumbling]

111
00:11:11,504 --> 00:11:13,798
Hurry! The wall is closing!

112
00:11:13,965 --> 00:11:15,592
Mondoshawan:
Here is your mission now:

113
00:11:15,758 --> 00:11:19,804
Pass your knowledge to the next priest
as it was passed on to you.

114
00:11:19,971 --> 00:11:23,600
I will do as you command,
but, please, hurry, you still have time.

115
00:11:23,766 --> 00:11:25,768
Mondoshawan: Time not important.

116
00:11:25,935 --> 00:11:28,438
Only life important.

117
00:11:33,776 --> 00:11:35,820
[♪♪♪]

118
00:11:42,327 --> 00:11:44,704
I will fulfill my mission!

119
00:11:44,871 --> 00:11:46,372
You can count on me!

120
00:11:50,293 --> 00:11:53,004
I will pass the knowledge
until your return!

121
00:12:14,943 --> 00:12:16,653
Man 1:
Deploy inter-ship stabilizers.

122
00:12:16,819 --> 00:12:19,447
Man 2: Power capacitors, check.
Man 3: Base modulation nominal.

123
00:12:19,614 --> 00:12:21,783
[Indistinct chatter]

124
00:12:21,950 --> 00:12:23,284
- Anything yet?
- No, sir.

125
00:12:23,451 --> 00:12:25,851
- Not even a temperature?
- The thermo-analyzers have jammed.

126
00:12:25,954 --> 00:12:28,373
One of them shows a million degrees,
the others minus 5000.

127
00:12:29,207 --> 00:12:30,625
Let's see it.

128
00:12:45,098 --> 00:12:47,308
[Controls beeping]

129
00:12:47,475 --> 00:12:49,185
It's taking shape.

130
00:13:07,704 --> 00:13:09,163
Send out a probe.

131
00:13:10,373 --> 00:13:14,961
Man: Ladies and gentlemen,
the president of the federated territories.

132
00:13:17,380 --> 00:13:19,924
On air with general staedert
in 30 seconds.

133
00:13:24,721 --> 00:13:26,347
[Gasps]

134
00:13:27,056 --> 00:13:30,226
Oh, I saved this seat for you, father.

135
00:13:32,270 --> 00:13:34,981
- President on the line, sir.
- We're in position, Mr. President.

136
00:13:35,148 --> 00:13:38,234
I have to address the supreme council
in 10 minutes. Just the facts, general.

137
00:13:38,401 --> 00:13:41,121
There are no results from the chemical
and molecular analysis as yet.

138
00:13:41,279 --> 00:13:42,739
All the calibers are overshot.

139
00:13:42,905 --> 00:13:44,741
We 're initiating
a thermonucleatic imaging.

140
00:13:44,907 --> 00:13:47,618
So, what you're saying is,
you don't know what this is.

141
00:13:47,785 --> 00:13:50,121
Not yet, sir. All we know is,
it just keeps getting bigger.

142
00:13:50,288 --> 00:13:51,372
Recommendation?

143
00:13:51,539 --> 00:13:54,584
My philosophy, Mr. President,
is shoot first and ask questions later.

144
00:13:54,751 --> 00:13:57,170
I don't like uninvited guests.

145
00:13:57,337 --> 00:13:59,756
- All right, then, staedert...
- Cornelius: Mr. President?

146
00:14:00,798 --> 00:14:02,133
Yes?

147
00:14:02,300 --> 00:14:06,262
Computer: Priest vito Cornelius,
expert of astrophenomenon.

148
00:14:06,429 --> 00:14:09,891
I have a different theory
to offer you, sir.

149
00:14:11,476 --> 00:14:12,643
You have 20 seconds.

150
00:14:13,561 --> 00:14:15,563
[♪♪♪]

151
00:14:19,233 --> 00:14:20,902
Imagine for a moment that this...

152
00:14:21,069 --> 00:14:24,280
Thing is not anything
that can be identified...

153
00:14:24,447 --> 00:14:26,783
Because it prefers not to be.

154
00:14:26,949 --> 00:14:30,620
Wherever there is life,
it brings death...

155
00:14:31,621 --> 00:14:35,458
- Because it is evil. Absolute evil.
- One more reason to shoot first.

156
00:14:35,625 --> 00:14:38,294
Evil begets evil, Mr. President.

157
00:14:38,461 --> 00:14:40,963
Shooting will only make it stronger.

158
00:14:41,464 --> 00:14:43,466
[Probe beeping]

159
00:14:45,009 --> 00:14:47,428
Probe will obtain its objective
in five seconds.

160
00:14:52,308 --> 00:14:53,935
Growth rate is at 27 percent.

161
00:14:54,102 --> 00:14:56,979
Your theory is interesting,
but we don't have time to go into that now.

162
00:14:57,146 --> 00:15:00,525
Time is of no importance, Mr. President.
Only life is important.

163
00:15:00,691 --> 00:15:03,277
You're right.
That's exactly what we're gonna do.

164
00:15:03,444 --> 00:15:06,489
We're gonna protect the life
of some 200 billion of my fellow citizens.

165
00:15:06,656 --> 00:15:08,199
General, you may fire when ready.

166
00:15:08,366 --> 00:15:11,577
Up-front loading of a 120-zr missile.
Marker lights on the objective.

167
00:15:17,583 --> 00:15:19,503
Its structure has just solidified
on the surface.

168
00:15:19,669 --> 00:15:23,381
I think it's anticipating the attack.
Anticipation denotes intelligence.

169
00:15:23,548 --> 00:15:27,593
The most terrible intelligence imaginable,
Mr. President.

170
00:15:32,974 --> 00:15:36,686
The ship is in combat formation.
Missiles are loaded, Mr. President.

171
00:15:36,853 --> 00:15:38,688
-Staedert. Staedert: Yes, sir.

172
00:15:38,855 --> 00:15:41,732
- I have a doubt.
- I don't, Mr. President.

173
00:15:53,870 --> 00:15:55,746
What happened?
Staedert, can you hear me?

174
00:15:55,913 --> 00:15:57,623
Staedert? What happened, staedert?

175
00:15:57,790 --> 00:16:00,334
- Did you destroy it?
- I'm about to, sir.

176
00:16:06,215 --> 00:16:08,968
The planet has increased
in diameter by 200 percent.

177
00:16:09,135 --> 00:16:10,595
It's moving towards the ship.

178
00:16:15,516 --> 00:16:18,227
What...? What do we have
that's bigger than 240?

179
00:16:18,394 --> 00:16:19,812
Nothing, sir.

180
00:16:20,563 --> 00:16:24,317
Staedert, do you hear me?
Get out of there.

181
00:16:24,484 --> 00:16:27,737
I don't want an incident.
Do you hear me, staedert?

182
00:16:27,904 --> 00:16:31,073
Get out of there.
Can you hear me, staedert?

183
00:16:31,240 --> 00:16:33,201
Do you understand? Listen.

184
00:16:33,367 --> 00:16:34,911
This is the president.
That's an order.

185
00:16:38,080 --> 00:16:40,291
Do you understand me?
Do you hear me?

186
00:16:40,458 --> 00:16:42,543
[Breaking up on radio]
Get out of there! Answer me!

187
00:16:47,089 --> 00:16:48,257
[Yells]

188
00:17:02,271 --> 00:17:04,774
[Groaning]

189
00:17:06,359 --> 00:17:07,652
[♪♪♪]

190
00:17:07,818 --> 00:17:09,487
Computer: Four a day.

191
00:17:11,072 --> 00:17:13,074
[Meowing]

192
00:17:22,124 --> 00:17:23,459
I'm trying.

193
00:17:24,293 --> 00:17:26,128
Computer: To quit is my goal.

194
00:17:26,295 --> 00:17:28,297
[Phone ringing]

195
00:17:29,215 --> 00:17:31,717
Hey, hey, hey!

196
00:17:31,884 --> 00:17:33,219
I'm up.

197
00:17:35,805 --> 00:17:37,306
All right, I'm up.

198
00:17:39,642 --> 00:17:42,311
Yeah. Yeah. Yes?

199
00:17:42,478 --> 00:17:44,730
Man [on phone]:
Hey, dog brain, finger here.

200
00:17:44,897 --> 00:17:47,066
- Hi, sweetie.
- I love you too, major...

201
00:17:47,233 --> 00:17:49,402
But you haven't called me that
since basic training.

202
00:17:49,569 --> 00:17:52,738
- I was talking to the cat.
- Oh, yeah, I forgot...

203
00:17:52,905 --> 00:17:55,366
You still prefer your cat
to the real thing.

204
00:17:55,533 --> 00:17:57,159
Korben:
At least the cat comes back.

205
00:17:57,326 --> 00:18:00,871
You still pining for that two-timing slut?
There are a million women out there.

206
00:18:01,038 --> 00:18:04,834
I don't want a million women.
I just want one.

207
00:18:05,501 --> 00:18:07,003
The perfect one.

208
00:18:07,169 --> 00:18:11,674
- It don't exist, major.
- Yeah, I know. Ugh.

209
00:18:11,841 --> 00:18:13,843
- What?
- Just found a picture of you.

210
00:18:14,010 --> 00:18:15,469
- Oh, how do ilook?
- Like shit.

211
00:18:15,636 --> 00:18:17,013
Must be an old picture.

212
00:18:17,179 --> 00:18:20,474
Listen, you gotta bring me your hack
for a six-month overhaul.

213
00:18:20,641 --> 00:18:21,851
- Negative.
- Asap.

214
00:18:22,184 --> 00:18:23,686
I don't need one.

215
00:18:23,853 --> 00:18:27,523
Hey, you forgetting who sat next to you
for 1000 missions? I know how you drive.

216
00:18:27,690 --> 00:18:32,194
Finger, I drive a cab now,
not a space fighter.

217
00:18:32,361 --> 00:18:36,032
Okay, so tell me. How many points
you got left on your license?

218
00:18:36,198 --> 00:18:38,367
Major, how many points?

219
00:18:38,534 --> 00:18:39,910
- At least 50.
- Heh-heh.

220
00:18:40,077 --> 00:18:42,538
Know what?
You gotta learn how to lie better.

221
00:18:42,705 --> 00:18:43,914
See you tonight.

222
00:18:48,878 --> 00:18:51,255
Female voice:
Welcome to paradise.

223
00:18:51,422 --> 00:18:53,062
Man [on TV]:
Welcome to fhloston paradise.

224
00:18:53,174 --> 00:18:56,135
It's Ruby rhod, your main man,
and I will tell you live at 5...

225
00:18:56,302 --> 00:18:59,597
The name of the winner of the
super-green gemini croquette contest!

226
00:18:59,764 --> 00:19:02,975
The winner will go with me
for two days to fhloston paradise.

227
00:19:03,142 --> 00:19:04,810
So tune in to radio cosmos.

228
00:19:04,977 --> 00:19:08,064
Don't watch it all day, sweetie.
It'll rot your brain.

229
00:19:08,230 --> 00:19:09,523
For a perfect world.

230
00:19:14,403 --> 00:19:16,572
- Give me the cash.
- Been here long?

231
00:19:16,739 --> 00:19:19,200
Yeah, long enough.
Come on, give me the cash.

232
00:19:19,367 --> 00:19:22,536
Is that a z-140? Alleviated titanium.

233
00:19:22,703 --> 00:19:25,498
- Neurocharged assault model.
- Yeah. Yeah.

234
00:19:25,665 --> 00:19:28,042
Hm. Good thing for me it's not loaded.

235
00:19:28,209 --> 00:19:29,460
[Laughing]

236
00:19:29,627 --> 00:19:32,421
- What do you mean, it's not loaded?
- Well, you have to...

237
00:19:32,922 --> 00:19:35,466
You have to push
that little yellow button to load it.

238
00:19:37,426 --> 00:19:39,095
[Laughs nervously]

239
00:19:39,261 --> 00:19:40,596
Take your time.

240
00:19:40,763 --> 00:19:42,390
Oh, god.

241
00:19:43,557 --> 00:19:45,184
You want me to...?

242
00:19:45,351 --> 00:19:46,769
Okay.

243
00:19:47,103 --> 00:19:48,437
[Gun cocks]

244
00:19:48,604 --> 00:19:49,939
- There you go.
- Aah!

245
00:19:50,106 --> 00:19:51,607
Give me the cash!

246
00:19:51,774 --> 00:19:53,442
[Gun whirs]

247
00:19:54,944 --> 00:19:56,320
Man:

248
00:19:58,280 --> 00:20:00,032
That's a very dangerous gun.

249
00:20:00,199 --> 00:20:03,452
You know, maybe you better let me
hang on to this one for you, huh?

250
00:20:04,412 --> 00:20:05,663
- You don't mind, do you?
- No.

251
00:20:05,830 --> 00:20:09,583
- You sure?
- No. Take it. I don't need it.

252
00:20:09,750 --> 00:20:11,752
[♪♪♪]

253
00:20:13,379 --> 00:20:14,797
[Speaks indistinctly]

254
00:20:14,964 --> 00:20:16,465
That's a very nice hat.

255
00:20:16,632 --> 00:20:18,592
You like it? Ungh!

256
00:20:18,759 --> 00:20:19,927
God!

257
00:20:26,058 --> 00:20:27,727
Computer:
Please enter your license.

258
00:20:27,893 --> 00:20:30,146
Yes, yes, just a minute.

259
00:20:31,439 --> 00:20:33,649
Welcome on board, Mr. Dallas.

260
00:20:34,108 --> 00:20:36,861
Good morning. Sleep well?
Yeah, me too.

261
00:20:37,445 --> 00:20:40,156
- I had a horrible nightmare.
- Propulsion 2x4.

262
00:20:44,452 --> 00:20:47,163
You have five points left
on your license.

263
00:20:47,329 --> 00:20:49,832
Yeah, thank you for reminding me.

264
00:20:51,375 --> 00:20:53,127
Have a nice day.

265
00:20:54,378 --> 00:20:55,713
Why not?

266
00:20:59,300 --> 00:21:01,302
[Car horns honking]

267
00:21:04,013 --> 00:21:05,306
You have 48 hours.

268
00:21:05,473 --> 00:21:08,476
That's the length of time it needs
to adapt itself to our living conditions.

269
00:21:08,642 --> 00:21:10,728
- And then?
- And then it will be too late.

270
00:21:10,895 --> 00:21:14,315
The goal of this thing is not
to fight over money or power...

271
00:21:16,192 --> 00:21:19,528
But to exterminate life.
All forms of life.

272
00:21:19,695 --> 00:21:22,615
So what you're telling me, father,
there's nothing that can stop this.

273
00:21:23,365 --> 00:21:25,367
There is only one thing.

274
00:21:29,872 --> 00:21:33,667
Cornelius: The mondoshawan have
the only weapon to defeat evil.

275
00:21:33,834 --> 00:21:35,878
Four elements...

276
00:21:36,378 --> 00:21:38,506
Gathered around a fifth...

277
00:21:38,881 --> 00:21:43,427
Supreme being, the ultimate warrior,
created to protect life.

278
00:21:43,594 --> 00:21:46,680
Together they produce what
the ancients called the light of creation.

279
00:21:46,847 --> 00:21:49,892
Able to bring life to the farthest reaches
of the universe.

280
00:21:50,601 --> 00:21:54,897
But if evil stands there...

281
00:21:56,565 --> 00:21:57,775
Then what?

282
00:21:57,942 --> 00:22:01,946
Then light turns to dark.
Life to death...

283
00:22:02,112 --> 00:22:03,572
Forever.

284
00:22:05,616 --> 00:22:08,077
Sir, there's a mondoshawan spaceship
at the frontier...

285
00:22:08,244 --> 00:22:10,579
Requesting permission
to enter our territory.

286
00:22:11,622 --> 00:22:15,417
President: Give it permission to enter
our territory with my warmest regards.

287
00:22:15,584 --> 00:22:16,836
Thank you.

288
00:22:17,002 --> 00:22:18,921
Man [on radio]:
Permission to enter granted.

289
00:22:21,590 --> 00:22:23,592
[♪♪♪]

290
00:22:39,942 --> 00:22:42,152
[Computer beeping]

291
00:23:18,814 --> 00:23:20,190
We are lost.

292
00:23:21,483 --> 00:23:23,444
Mangalore:
Aknot, we are connected to earth.

293
00:23:23,611 --> 00:23:25,154
[Growls]

294
00:23:25,738 --> 00:23:27,656
[Comm beeping]

295
00:23:27,823 --> 00:23:29,408
Mr. Zorg's office.

296
00:23:29,575 --> 00:23:30,910
Aknot [on comm]: It's aknot,

297
00:23:31,327 --> 00:23:34,622
Zorg:
I'm so glad to hear you, aknot.

298
00:23:34,788 --> 00:23:37,207
The mission is accomplished.

299
00:23:38,167 --> 00:23:41,337
You'll have what you asked for
in a few hours.

300
00:23:42,171 --> 00:23:44,590
Good. I'll meet you at my factory.

301
00:23:45,007 --> 00:23:47,217
The attack was launched
by two unregistered warships.

302
00:23:47,384 --> 00:23:49,279
Close all borders and declare
a state of general alert.

303
00:23:49,303 --> 00:23:50,346
Yes, sir.

304
00:23:50,512 --> 00:23:51,865
Try to make contact
with the mondoshawans.

305
00:23:51,889 --> 00:23:53,283
- We owe them an explanation.
- Sir.

306
00:23:53,307 --> 00:23:57,102
Three hundred years of waiting
for nothing.

307
00:23:57,603 --> 00:23:59,438
Father,
you should go home now and rest.

308
00:24:01,106 --> 00:24:02,733
The mondoshawan...

309
00:24:03,192 --> 00:24:05,194
I am their contact on earth.
They will come for me.

310
00:24:05,361 --> 00:24:08,906
Father, this is government business now.
I will keep you informed.

311
00:24:09,073 --> 00:24:11,158
[♪♪♪]

312
00:24:11,867 --> 00:24:14,370
The rescue team has reported
from the mondoshawan crash site.

313
00:24:14,536 --> 00:24:15,955
Any survivors?

314
00:24:16,121 --> 00:24:17,414
Only one.

315
00:24:20,709 --> 00:24:22,211
Munro:
That what you call a survivor?

316
00:24:22,378 --> 00:24:24,463
A few cells are still alive.
It's more than I need.

317
00:24:24,630 --> 00:24:26,150
- Have you identified it?
- We tried...

318
00:24:26,215 --> 00:24:27,815
But the computer went off the charts.

319
00:24:27,841 --> 00:24:30,719
You see, normal human beings
have 40 DNA memo groups...

320
00:24:30,886 --> 00:24:33,486
Which is more than enough
for any species to perpetuate itself.

321
00:24:33,639 --> 00:24:36,558
This has 200,000 memo groups.

322
00:24:41,146 --> 00:24:45,776
- Sounds like a freak of nature to me.
- Yeah, can't wait to meet him.

323
00:24:53,909 --> 00:24:55,202
You okay, general? Over here.

324
00:24:56,161 --> 00:24:57,579
Excuse me.

325
00:25:02,626 --> 00:25:05,045
Okay, general,
I want to show you something here.

326
00:25:05,671 --> 00:25:08,424
This is a normal human DNA chain, okay?

327
00:25:08,590 --> 00:25:10,759
You, me, anybody, right?

328
00:25:10,926 --> 00:25:12,177
Watch this.

329
00:25:13,303 --> 00:25:16,598
The compositional elements
of his DNA chain are the same as ours.

330
00:25:16,765 --> 00:25:20,019
There's more of them, tightly packed,
with infinite genetic knowledge.

331
00:25:20,185 --> 00:25:22,855
Almost like this being was engineered.

332
00:25:27,026 --> 00:25:28,426
- Is there any danger?
- No, no, no.

333
00:25:28,569 --> 00:25:30,529
We put it through
the cellular hygiene detector.

334
00:25:30,696 --> 00:25:33,240
The cell is, for lack of a better word...

335
00:25:33,407 --> 00:25:34,783
Perfect.

336
00:25:36,076 --> 00:25:38,078
Okay, go ahead.

337
00:25:38,245 --> 00:25:39,955
But Mr. Perfect better be polite.

338
00:25:40,122 --> 00:25:42,207
Othen/vise, I turn him into cat food.

339
00:25:42,708 --> 00:25:43,959
Activate it.

340
00:25:44,835 --> 00:25:46,837
[♪♪♪]

341
00:26:15,491 --> 00:26:16,825
Tissue processing.

342
00:26:30,547 --> 00:26:33,634
Ten seconds to ultraviolet protection.

343
00:26:39,556 --> 00:26:41,266
Mactilburgh:
This is the last phase.

344
00:26:41,433 --> 00:26:43,313
The cells are bombarded
by greasy solar atoms...

345
00:26:43,435 --> 00:26:45,604
Which forces the body
to react to protect itself.

346
00:26:45,771 --> 00:26:47,231
That means growing skin.

347
00:26:47,397 --> 00:26:48,774
Wonderful.

348
00:26:54,279 --> 00:26:56,406
Reconstruction complete.

349
00:26:59,785 --> 00:27:01,495
Remove the shield.

350
00:27:10,003 --> 00:27:12,256
I told you. Perfect.

351
00:27:20,806 --> 00:27:21,974
Thermal bandages.

352
00:27:26,436 --> 00:27:30,816
I'd, um, like to take a few pictures...

353
00:27:31,733 --> 00:27:33,110
For the archives.

354
00:27:39,741 --> 00:27:41,410
[Gasps]

355
00:27:41,577 --> 00:27:43,537
[Grunting]

356
00:27:53,297 --> 00:27:54,756
[Growls]

357
00:27:54,923 --> 00:27:56,258
[Panting]

358
00:28:29,875 --> 00:28:31,877
[Speaking in divine language]

359
00:28:33,754 --> 00:28:35,255
- What's she saying?
- I don't know.

360
00:28:35,422 --> 00:28:36,965
Activate the phonic detector.

361
00:28:47,726 --> 00:28:48,977
Heh.

362
00:28:49,645 --> 00:28:51,855
Is, uh...? Is that thing solid?

363
00:28:52,022 --> 00:28:53,398
- Unbreakable.
- Good.

364
00:29:03,659 --> 00:29:05,327
If you want out...

365
00:29:05,494 --> 00:29:09,164
You're going to have to learn
to develop those communication skills.

366
00:29:16,672 --> 00:29:18,006
[Breathing heavily]

367
00:29:20,092 --> 00:29:22,386
[Growling]

368
00:29:23,303 --> 00:29:24,513
[Grunts]

369
00:29:27,224 --> 00:29:28,558
General alert.

370
00:29:28,725 --> 00:29:30,310
[Alarm wailing]

371
00:29:30,477 --> 00:29:32,771
[Man speaking indistinctly]

372
00:29:41,154 --> 00:29:43,156
[♪♪♪]

373
00:29:55,252 --> 00:29:56,712
Perfect.

374
00:29:57,129 --> 00:29:59,131
[Alarm buzzing]

375
00:30:03,510 --> 00:30:05,321
Two men with me.
The rest in the main ventilation.

376
00:30:05,345 --> 00:30:06,388
Okay, sir.

377
00:30:25,532 --> 00:30:26,616
This way.

378
00:31:01,234 --> 00:31:03,987
Officer 1:
Okay, lady, stay calm.

379
00:31:04,154 --> 00:31:05,739
This is the police.

380
00:31:06,239 --> 00:31:07,991
There's nowhere else to go.

381
00:31:08,158 --> 00:31:12,120
So you're gonna slowly turn around
and put your hands on the floor.

382
00:31:12,287 --> 00:31:13,830
Do you understand me?

383
00:31:17,292 --> 00:31:18,543
She doesn't.

384
00:31:37,521 --> 00:31:38,730
[Gasps]

385
00:31:43,485 --> 00:31:45,112
I think we need a flying unit here.

386
00:31:47,114 --> 00:31:51,118
Officer 2 [on loudspeaker]:
This is the police. This is the police.

387
00:31:51,284 --> 00:31:53,245
We are processing your identification.

388
00:31:53,412 --> 00:31:55,872
Please put your arms up
and follow our instructions.

389
00:32:08,009 --> 00:32:09,219
She has no file.

390
00:32:22,023 --> 00:32:24,025
[Police siren blaring]

391
00:32:26,194 --> 00:32:27,696
[Korben yells]

392
00:32:32,826 --> 00:32:34,327
Computer:
You just had an accident.

393
00:32:34,494 --> 00:32:37,414
Yes, I know I just had an accident,
you daffy bastard!

394
00:32:39,082 --> 00:32:41,352
- You have one point left on your license.
- You have one point...

395
00:32:41,376 --> 00:32:42,919
Look out!

396
00:32:43,086 --> 00:32:44,671
No, no! Left!

397
00:32:49,009 --> 00:32:50,886
I can't believe it. Shit.

398
00:32:53,346 --> 00:32:54,514
[Grunts]

399
00:32:56,725 --> 00:32:58,185
Any survivors?

400
00:32:59,019 --> 00:33:01,021
[♪♪♪]

401
00:33:08,904 --> 00:33:10,030
You okay?

402
00:33:14,409 --> 00:33:15,952
[Chuckles]

403
00:33:16,453 --> 00:33:18,455
[Speaking in divine language]

404
00:33:37,849 --> 00:33:38,892
Boom.

405
00:33:39,059 --> 00:33:41,520
Boom. Yeah, I understand "boom."

406
00:33:42,270 --> 00:33:43,980
Bada boom.

407
00:33:44,606 --> 00:33:47,234
Big. Big bada boom.

408
00:33:47,400 --> 00:33:48,568
Big...

409
00:33:48,735 --> 00:33:50,320
Bada big boom.

410
00:33:51,947 --> 00:33:54,741
- Yeah, big bada boom.
- Bada boom.

411
00:33:54,908 --> 00:33:57,244
Big boom. Big bada boom.

412
00:34:00,622 --> 00:34:01,998
You're lucky you're not dead.

413
00:34:02,165 --> 00:34:03,792
[Siren blares]

414
00:34:05,752 --> 00:34:07,837
Officer [on loudspeaker]:
This is a police control.

415
00:34:08,004 --> 00:34:10,799
Please keep your hands on the wheel.

416
00:34:10,966 --> 00:34:13,969
You have an unauthorized passenger
in your vehicle.

417
00:34:14,135 --> 00:34:16,054
We are going to arrest her.

418
00:34:16,221 --> 00:34:17,889
Thank you for your cooperation.

419
00:34:18,056 --> 00:34:19,474
Sorry, honey.

420
00:34:19,641 --> 00:34:21,560
Looks like this is your ride.

421
00:34:21,726 --> 00:34:23,436
Open the door.

422
00:34:24,604 --> 00:34:26,856
- Akta.
- Better do what they say.

423
00:34:28,900 --> 00:34:30,777
Sorry.

424
00:34:30,944 --> 00:34:32,946
[♪♪♪]

425
00:34:40,412 --> 00:34:41,871
[Sighs]

426
00:34:52,966 --> 00:34:55,093
"Please...

427
00:34:55,260 --> 00:34:57,304
Help."

428
00:34:57,470 --> 00:34:59,156
I've only got one point left
on my license...

429
00:34:59,180 --> 00:35:03,018
And I need that to get back to the garage
and get the cab a six-month overhaul.

430
00:35:03,184 --> 00:35:04,769
You understand?

431
00:35:06,438 --> 00:35:08,732
Can you please open
the passenger door?

432
00:35:09,858 --> 00:35:12,652
Ple... please...

433
00:35:14,446 --> 00:35:16,364
Help.

434
00:35:17,991 --> 00:35:19,492
I can't.

435
00:35:24,122 --> 00:35:25,562
Officer [on loudspeaker]:
I repeat...

436
00:35:25,707 --> 00:35:27,834
Can you please open
your passenger door?

437
00:35:28,001 --> 00:35:30,211
Yeah, yeah, sure.

438
00:35:30,378 --> 00:35:31,838
Why not?

439
00:35:45,935 --> 00:35:47,604
Thank you for your cooperation.

440
00:35:50,857 --> 00:35:52,108
Help.

441
00:35:53,693 --> 00:35:55,695
Ko rb e n:
Finger's gonna kill me.

442
00:36:03,745 --> 00:36:05,246
Emergency! Emergency!

443
00:36:05,413 --> 00:36:07,475
Computer: One point has been
removed from your license.

444
00:36:07,499 --> 00:36:09,376
Yes, I know!

445
00:36:09,542 --> 00:36:10,919
On your license.

446
00:36:14,589 --> 00:36:16,424
This is so stupid.

447
00:36:17,759 --> 00:36:20,196
Woman [on radio]: All units assist
in pursuit of yellow cab, level 10.

448
00:36:20,220 --> 00:36:22,138
Unit 47, we're on the way...

449
00:36:22,305 --> 00:36:23,640
As soon as we finish lunch.

450
00:36:26,685 --> 00:36:28,603
Two golden menus.

451
00:36:29,062 --> 00:36:31,773
Officer 1: Thank you.
Officer 2: I'm too old, too tired...

452
00:36:31,940 --> 00:36:34,484
And too hungry
to go chasing some hot rod.

453
00:36:36,277 --> 00:36:37,737
Thank you so much.

454
00:36:41,408 --> 00:36:43,743
And I'm definitely too thirsty.

455
00:36:43,910 --> 00:36:46,079
Korben: Look out!

456
00:36:50,291 --> 00:36:51,793
We got lucky.

457
00:36:53,128 --> 00:36:55,755
If they don't chase you after a mile,
they don't chase you.

458
00:36:55,922 --> 00:36:57,924
[♪♪♪]

459
00:36:59,050 --> 00:37:01,052
[Sirens blaring]

460
00:37:03,012 --> 00:37:04,180
Maybe it's two miles.

461
00:37:05,724 --> 00:37:07,142
Hang on.

462
00:37:14,858 --> 00:37:16,693
[Yelling in divine language]

463
00:37:16,860 --> 00:37:19,487
Look, lady, I only speak two languages:
English and bad English!

464
00:37:21,906 --> 00:37:22,949
Run an ID.

465
00:37:25,660 --> 00:37:29,789
Don't get me wrong, I'm for conversation,
but maybe you could shut up for a minute!

466
00:37:31,499 --> 00:37:33,209
I get nothing. He's got a scan blocker.

467
00:37:33,376 --> 00:37:36,045
Means he's a car thief. Blast him.

468
00:37:40,425 --> 00:37:42,425
I don't know what you did
to piss these guys off...

469
00:37:44,512 --> 00:37:46,890
But they are really pissed off!
Hold on!

470
00:38:04,491 --> 00:38:06,242
I think we're safe for a while.

471
00:38:31,100 --> 00:38:33,728
You want to play it soft?
We'll play it soft.

472
00:38:33,895 --> 00:38:37,232
You want to play it hard?
Let's play it hard.

473
00:38:41,736 --> 00:38:43,363
[Speaking in divine language]

474
00:38:47,700 --> 00:38:49,994
We make it to the fog,
we'll be all right.

475
00:38:52,580 --> 00:38:54,332
If we make the fog.

476
00:39:12,225 --> 00:39:15,103
How do they expect us
to find anything in this shit?

477
00:39:20,733 --> 00:39:24,696
We're just gonna wait here for a little while
until things quiet down, if you don't mind.

478
00:39:25,905 --> 00:39:27,073
Hey.

479
00:39:38,626 --> 00:39:39,836
Shit.

480
00:39:49,095 --> 00:39:50,555
You okay?

481
00:39:52,432 --> 00:39:53,600
Priest.

482
00:39:54,142 --> 00:39:56,936
You don't need a priest, you just
need a doctor. You'll be all right.

483
00:39:57,103 --> 00:39:59,939
Vito Cornelius.

484
00:40:00,106 --> 00:40:01,149
What?

485
00:40:01,316 --> 00:40:02,984
Priest.

486
00:40:06,195 --> 00:40:07,238
Yes?

487
00:40:07,822 --> 00:40:10,116
I'm, uh, looking for a priest.

488
00:40:10,283 --> 00:40:12,994
Weddings are one floor down, my son.
Congratulations.

489
00:40:15,413 --> 00:40:17,332
She's not my bride. She's my fare.

490
00:40:17,498 --> 00:40:19,417
She's looking for a priest
named vito Cornelius.

491
00:40:19,584 --> 00:40:21,502
The phone book said he lived here.

492
00:40:21,669 --> 00:40:24,714
Yes, that's me,
but I don't know who she is.

493
00:40:24,881 --> 00:40:27,508
Nobody knows who she is.
No file, no ID, nothing.

494
00:40:27,675 --> 00:40:29,677
She's got a tattoo on this arm here.

495
00:40:30,887 --> 00:40:32,555
Tattoo?

496
00:40:35,058 --> 00:40:37,518
[♪♪♪]

497
00:40:39,395 --> 00:40:40,772
[Stammers]

498
00:40:42,482 --> 00:40:43,900
Fifth...

499
00:40:44,275 --> 00:40:45,735
Element.

500
00:40:51,199 --> 00:40:52,909
Finger's gonna kill me.

501
00:40:53,076 --> 00:40:55,662
- Hey! Wake up.
- Who are you?

502
00:40:55,828 --> 00:40:58,122
Brought the girl, remember?
The redhead.

503
00:41:00,416 --> 00:41:04,420
She just dropped in on me.
Started speaking this bizarre language.

504
00:41:04,587 --> 00:41:06,965
It's not bizarre.
It's the divine language.

505
00:41:07,131 --> 00:41:08,883
- The ancient language...
- Okay.

506
00:41:09,050 --> 00:41:12,178
Spoken throughout the universe
before time was time. He...

507
00:41:13,972 --> 00:41:15,014
He's a she.

508
00:41:15,181 --> 00:41:16,516
You noticed that, huh?

509
00:41:22,563 --> 00:41:23,898
Heh.

510
00:41:24,065 --> 00:41:26,401
- It's a miracle.
- Miracle she's not dead.

511
00:41:26,567 --> 00:41:28,236
We've not a moment to lose.
Wake her up.

512
00:41:28,403 --> 00:41:33,783
But gently, because this woman is
mankind's most precious possession.

513
00:41:33,950 --> 00:41:35,576
She is perfect.

514
00:41:37,954 --> 00:41:39,956
[♪♪♪]

515
00:41:40,123 --> 00:41:41,666
Perfect.

516
00:41:48,673 --> 00:41:49,924
More dignified.

517
00:41:50,091 --> 00:41:51,634
Hey, lady...

518
00:41:51,801 --> 00:41:53,052
Wake up.

519
00:42:04,439 --> 00:42:05,481
[Gun cocks]

520
00:42:05,648 --> 00:42:08,085
You're right, I shouldn't have done that.
I shouldn't have done that.

521
00:42:08,109 --> 00:42:10,570
It was wrong to kiss you.
He said to wake you gently.

522
00:42:10,737 --> 00:42:12,196
You're right. You're right.

523
00:42:12,363 --> 00:42:14,073
[Speaking in divine language]

524
00:42:14,699 --> 00:42:17,618
Just thought you might
remember me from the cab.

525
00:42:18,202 --> 00:42:20,580
Remember? "Bada boom"?

526
00:42:21,706 --> 00:42:23,416
- "Big bada boom"?
- Boom?

527
00:42:23,583 --> 00:42:26,335
Boom. Big bada boom.
In the cab. Here, look.

528
00:42:26,502 --> 00:42:29,005
I drive a cab. This is me.

529
00:42:29,172 --> 00:42:30,840
Korben Dallas.

530
00:42:31,716 --> 00:42:33,051
Korben. You understand?

531
00:42:33,718 --> 00:42:35,845
Here. Take it, go ahead.

532
00:42:36,763 --> 00:42:38,848
You can call me
when you learn how to speak English.

533
00:42:40,641 --> 00:42:42,226
Oop. Ah.

534
00:42:42,393 --> 00:42:43,811
Just kidding. Kidding.

535
00:42:46,314 --> 00:42:47,774
And you... what is your name?

536
00:42:50,651 --> 00:42:52,236
Korben.

537
00:42:54,739 --> 00:42:57,867
Leeloo minai lekarariba-laminai-tchai
ekbat de sebat.

538
00:42:58,868 --> 00:43:00,661
Good. That's...

539
00:43:01,329 --> 00:43:02,955
That whole thing's your name, huh?

540
00:43:04,207 --> 00:43:05,875
Do you have a, uh...

541
00:43:07,001 --> 00:43:08,252
A shorter name?

542
00:43:08,419 --> 00:43:11,089
Not "yeah, yeah, yeah, ooh."

543
00:43:11,255 --> 00:43:12,507
Shon.

544
00:43:14,675 --> 00:43:15,885
[Whispers] Korben Dallas.

545
00:43:19,055 --> 00:43:20,306
Leeloo.

546
00:43:20,473 --> 00:43:22,350
[♪♪♪]

547
00:43:22,517 --> 00:43:23,851
Leeloo.

548
00:43:24,685 --> 00:43:26,145
[In normal voice]
Korben, leeloo.

549
00:43:26,521 --> 00:43:28,189
Leeloo, korben.

550
00:43:34,195 --> 00:43:36,739
[Gasping]

551
00:43:36,906 --> 00:43:39,242
[Laughing]

552
00:43:45,998 --> 00:43:47,792
Father, are you sure
she's a supreme being?

553
00:43:47,959 --> 00:43:49,752
Absolutely sure.

554
00:43:49,919 --> 00:43:52,672
Old friends. Okay. Yeah, you're right.

555
00:43:52,839 --> 00:43:56,217
Listen, do you think you could ask her
if I could have the gun back, please?

556
00:43:56,384 --> 00:43:58,636
- What's your name?
- Korben Dallas.

557
00:43:59,595 --> 00:44:02,056
Thank you, Mr. Dallas, for all your help.
Thank you so much.

558
00:44:02,223 --> 00:44:04,225
You've been so kind,
but now the girl needs rest...

559
00:44:04,392 --> 00:44:06,561
Because she's been on a long trip.

560
00:44:06,727 --> 00:44:09,105
Yes, I know.
I was there when she landed.

561
00:44:09,856 --> 00:44:11,482
Wait, wait, hey. Wait, wait, father.

562
00:44:11,649 --> 00:44:15,153
She said something I didn't understand.
Well, I didn't understand any of it...

563
00:44:15,319 --> 00:44:19,073
- But what does "ekto gamat" mean?
- "Never without my permission."

564
00:44:19,824 --> 00:44:21,409
That's what I thought.

565
00:44:29,625 --> 00:44:31,502
I shouldn't have kissed her.

566
00:44:34,255 --> 00:44:36,257
[Cat meowing]

567
00:44:36,757 --> 00:44:39,927
Oh, no. I'm so sorry.
I forgot your food.

568
00:44:40,094 --> 00:44:41,929
[Phone ringing]

569
00:44:42,096 --> 00:44:44,432
How about some nice Thai food
to apologize, huh?

570
00:44:44,599 --> 00:44:46,601
Yeah, yeah, hold on. What?

571
00:44:46,767 --> 00:44:49,228
Finger [on phone]:
Hey, buddy, I'm waiting all day here.

572
00:44:49,395 --> 00:44:51,105
- Finger.
- Where is the cab?

573
00:44:51,272 --> 00:44:53,065
Car's running fine.
Purring like a kitten.

574
00:44:53,232 --> 00:44:55,109
"Fine. "What "fine"?

575
00:44:55,276 --> 00:44:58,112
[Know you, Dallas.
"Fine" ain't in your vocabula'y-

576
00:44:58,279 --> 00:45:00,573
come on, you can tell
your old buddy finger what happened.

577
00:45:00,740 --> 00:45:02,783
- What? You save the planet?
- Listen.

578
00:45:02,950 --> 00:45:05,745
You dinged the Fender again. Right?
You dinged the goddamn Fender.

579
00:45:05,912 --> 00:45:10,625
Finger, I was on my way over to see you
and a big fare fell in my lap.

580
00:45:10,791 --> 00:45:13,628
You know, one of these really big fares
that you just can't resist.

581
00:45:13,794 --> 00:45:16,088
Oh. How big?

582
00:45:16,255 --> 00:45:18,257
[♪♪♪]

583
00:45:21,010 --> 00:45:22,595
[Moans]

584
00:45:24,472 --> 00:45:26,307
Five-nine...

585
00:45:26,891 --> 00:45:28,142
Blue eyes...

586
00:45:28,309 --> 00:45:30,311
Long legs, great skin.

587
00:45:30,645 --> 00:45:32,480
You know. Perfect.

588
00:45:34,398 --> 00:45:38,194
And this, uh, perfect fare,
she got a name?

589
00:45:40,655 --> 00:45:42,114
Leeloo.

590
00:45:49,372 --> 00:45:50,665
What's she doing?

591
00:45:50,831 --> 00:45:53,834
Learning our history,
the last 5000 years that she's missed.

592
00:45:54,001 --> 00:45:55,628
Been asleep for quite a while, you know.

593
00:45:59,131 --> 00:46:01,259
[Imitating martial arts yell]

594
00:46:01,425 --> 00:46:02,635
[Chuckles]

595
00:46:07,932 --> 00:46:11,018
Father, I know she's been through a lot,
but we don't have much time.

596
00:46:11,185 --> 00:46:12,311
Yes, you're right.

597
00:46:14,855 --> 00:46:17,566
Chicken. Good.

598
00:46:21,070 --> 00:46:22,655
Chicken.

599
00:46:27,326 --> 00:46:30,705
I'm really sorry to interrupt you...

600
00:46:30,871 --> 00:46:32,498
But the case...

601
00:46:32,665 --> 00:46:34,375
With the stones...

602
00:46:35,543 --> 00:46:36,585
Where is it?

603
00:46:36,752 --> 00:46:38,796
[Speaking in divine language]

604
00:46:42,758 --> 00:46:45,553
Who in god's name
would do such a thing?

605
00:46:45,720 --> 00:46:47,722
[♪♪♪]

606
00:46:50,474 --> 00:46:53,602
Excuse me, sir. The council is worried
about the economy heating up.

607
00:46:53,769 --> 00:46:56,439
They wondered
if it'd be possible to fire 500,000.

608
00:46:56,605 --> 00:46:59,442
Maybe from one of the smaller companies
where no one would notice...

609
00:46:59,608 --> 00:47:01,068
Like one of the cab companies.

610
00:47:01,235 --> 00:47:03,112
Zorg: Fire one million.

611
00:47:03,279 --> 00:47:05,865
But 500,000...

612
00:47:10,077 --> 00:47:12,580
One million. Fine, sir.

613
00:47:12,997 --> 00:47:14,790
Sorry to have disturbed you.

614
00:47:15,249 --> 00:47:17,376
[Footsteps walking]

615
00:47:17,543 --> 00:47:19,545
[Footsteps running]

616
00:47:24,425 --> 00:47:25,760
Oh, it's, uh...

617
00:47:25,926 --> 00:47:27,970
- It's for the supreme...
- Yes, yes, yes.

618
00:47:29,555 --> 00:47:31,223
Oh, sorry. Uh...

619
00:47:32,099 --> 00:47:36,437
I didn't know your size, and I found you
this makeup box, okay?

620
00:47:36,604 --> 00:47:39,690
- You just put it like that.
- Thank you.

621
00:47:39,857 --> 00:47:42,193
Yes, there was a man with a limp...

622
00:47:42,818 --> 00:47:45,946
Came here about a month ago
asking questions about the stones.

623
00:47:46,113 --> 00:47:47,531
He said he was an art dealer.

624
00:47:48,949 --> 00:47:50,493
[Speaking in divine language]

625
00:47:50,659 --> 00:47:52,411
What was his name?

626
00:47:54,705 --> 00:47:55,956
I'm so bad with names.

627
00:48:02,296 --> 00:48:05,758
- They really make her...
- Perfect, I know.

628
00:48:05,925 --> 00:48:07,927
[Speaking in divine language]

629
00:48:10,054 --> 00:48:11,555
What did she say?

630
00:48:13,265 --> 00:48:15,768
Cornelius: She says
she knows exactly where they are.

631
00:48:19,313 --> 00:48:23,150
My dear aknot, how about those
two little planes that you borrowed?

632
00:48:24,068 --> 00:48:27,154
Aknot, is that you? What an ugly face.

633
00:48:27,321 --> 00:48:28,781
It doesn't suit you.

634
00:48:29,365 --> 00:48:30,991
Take it off.

635
00:48:33,244 --> 00:48:34,495
That's better.

636
00:48:34,662 --> 00:48:36,455
Never be ashamed of who you are.

637
00:48:36,622 --> 00:48:38,499
You're warriors. Be proud.

638
00:48:38,666 --> 00:48:41,669
So what if the federal government
scattered your people to the wind.

639
00:48:41,836 --> 00:48:44,964
What doesn't kill you
makes you stronger.

640
00:48:45,131 --> 00:48:48,759
Your time for revenge
is at hand. Voila.

641
00:48:51,137 --> 00:48:53,139
[Mangalores grunting]

642
00:48:53,305 --> 00:48:56,725
It's light. Handle's adjustable for easy
carrying. Good for righties and lefties.

643
00:48:56,892 --> 00:48:58,936
Breaks down into four parts,
undetectable by X-ray.

644
00:48:59,103 --> 00:49:01,063
Ideal for quick, discreet interventions.

645
00:49:01,230 --> 00:49:02,648
A word on firepower:

646
00:49:02,815 --> 00:49:06,360
Titanium recharger, 3000-round clip
with bursts of 3 to 300.

647
00:49:06,527 --> 00:49:09,280
With the replay button,
another Zorg invention, it's even easier.

648
00:49:12,658 --> 00:49:15,494
And replay sends every following shot
to the same location.

649
00:49:16,162 --> 00:49:18,622
[Mangalores yelling]

650
00:49:22,460 --> 00:49:25,880
And to finish the job,
all the Zorg oldies but goldies.

651
00:49:26,630 --> 00:49:27,673
Rocket launcher.

652
00:49:29,925 --> 00:49:33,012
Arrow launcher with exploding
or poisonous gas heads.

653
00:49:34,472 --> 00:49:37,016
Very practical.
Our famous net launcher.

654
00:49:38,601 --> 00:49:40,019
The always-efficient flamethrower.

655
00:49:44,398 --> 00:49:45,441
My favorite.

656
00:49:46,025 --> 00:49:50,529
And for the grand finale,
the all-new ice-cube system.

657
00:49:57,161 --> 00:49:58,996
[Mangalores applauding
and grunting]

658
00:49:59,163 --> 00:50:02,541
Four full crates,
delivered right on time.

659
00:50:03,417 --> 00:50:07,379
And what about you, my dear aknot?
Did you bring me what I asked you for?

660
00:50:15,763 --> 00:50:17,431
Magnificent.

661
00:50:24,396 --> 00:50:26,649
This case is empty.

662
00:50:26,815 --> 00:50:28,108
[Laughing]

663
00:50:28,275 --> 00:50:30,444
- What do you mean, empty?
- Empty...

664
00:50:30,611 --> 00:50:32,613
The opposite of full.

665
00:50:32,780 --> 00:50:36,283
This case is supposed to be full!

666
00:50:38,410 --> 00:50:39,954
Anyone care to explain?

667
00:50:40,120 --> 00:50:42,039
[Speaking in divine language]

668
00:50:42,206 --> 00:50:46,252
The guardians gave the stones
to someone that they could trust.

669
00:50:49,421 --> 00:50:51,423
Who took another route.

670
00:50:52,925 --> 00:50:55,678
She's supposed
to contact this person...

671
00:50:55,844 --> 00:50:57,429
In a hotel.

672
00:51:01,642 --> 00:51:04,645
And she's looking for the address. Easy.

673
00:51:06,605 --> 00:51:07,856
Dot.

674
00:51:08,023 --> 00:51:09,650
[Computer beeping]

675
00:51:12,236 --> 00:51:14,989
It's planet fhloston,
in the angel constellation.

676
00:51:15,948 --> 00:51:19,577
- Ah. We're saved.
- I'm screwed.

677
00:51:19,743 --> 00:51:22,037
You asked for a case.
We brought you a case.

678
00:51:22,204 --> 00:51:24,540
A case with four stones in it!

679
00:51:24,707 --> 00:51:27,126
Not one or two or three, but four!

680
00:51:27,293 --> 00:51:28,502
Four stones!

681
00:51:28,669 --> 00:51:31,463
What the hell am I supposed to do
with an empty case?

682
00:51:31,630 --> 00:51:33,841
We are warriors, not merchants.

683
00:51:34,008 --> 00:51:37,136
But you can still count!
Look, it's easy. Look at my fingers.

684
00:51:37,303 --> 00:51:38,762
Four stones, four crates.

685
00:51:38,929 --> 00:51:42,516
Zero stones, zero crates!

686
00:51:42,683 --> 00:51:44,163
Pack everything up!
We're out of here!

687
00:51:44,560 --> 00:51:45,894
[Roars]

688
00:51:46,061 --> 00:51:47,313
[Guns cocking]

689
00:51:47,479 --> 00:51:49,565
Aknot: We risked our lives.

690
00:51:49,732 --> 00:51:53,652
I believe a little
compensation is in order.

691
00:51:53,819 --> 00:51:57,990
Oh. So you are merchants after all.

692
00:51:59,366 --> 00:52:01,952
Leave him one crate for the cause.

693
00:52:05,039 --> 00:52:07,750
I don't like warriors.
Too narrow-minded, no subtlety...

694
00:52:07,916 --> 00:52:11,170
And worse, they fight
for hopeless causes, honor.

695
00:52:11,337 --> 00:52:14,214
Honor's killed millions of people.
Hasn't saved a single one.

696
00:52:14,381 --> 00:52:16,842
Tell you what I do like, though: A killer.

697
00:52:17,009 --> 00:52:20,512
A dyed-in-the-wool killer, cold-blooded,
clean, methodical, and thorough.

698
00:52:20,679 --> 00:52:22,681
Now, a real killer,
when he picked up the zf-1

699
00:52:22,848 --> 00:52:26,268
would've immediately asked about
the red button on the bottom of the gun.

700
00:52:26,435 --> 00:52:28,437
[♪♪♪]

701
00:52:44,745 --> 00:52:46,121
Bring me the priest.

702
00:52:48,791 --> 00:52:51,311
I got everything here we need
to know about fhloston paradise...

703
00:52:51,377 --> 00:52:53,188
And a detailed blueprint
of the entire hotel.

704
00:52:53,212 --> 00:52:56,215
Good work, my son. Now all we've got
to do is find a way of getting there.

705
00:52:56,382 --> 00:52:59,062
It's not gonna be easy. There's
a charity ball on fhloston tomorrow.

706
00:52:59,093 --> 00:53:02,489
Flights are full, and with the celebrities,
the hotel will be guarded like a fortress.

707
00:53:02,513 --> 00:53:04,113
But there must be a way
of getting there.

708
00:53:06,975 --> 00:53:08,477
[Knocking on door]

709
00:53:10,604 --> 00:53:11,939
I'll get it.

710
00:53:13,524 --> 00:53:14,566
Weddings?

711
00:53:17,277 --> 00:53:18,362
Not really.

712
00:53:18,529 --> 00:53:21,365
- Mr. Zorg would like to talk to you.
- Mister who?

713
00:53:21,532 --> 00:53:23,117
Mr. Zorg.

714
00:53:23,784 --> 00:53:27,204
Zorg:
Jean-Baptiste Emmanuel Zorg.

715
00:53:30,958 --> 00:53:33,085
It's nice to see you again, father.

716
00:53:33,252 --> 00:53:35,629
Ah, I remember you now.

717
00:53:36,130 --> 00:53:38,716
The so-called art dealer.

718
00:53:38,882 --> 00:53:42,928
I'm glad you got your memory back,
because you're gonna need it.

719
00:53:45,097 --> 00:53:46,473
Where are the stones?

720
00:53:47,433 --> 00:53:50,644
I don't know. And even if I did know,
I wouldn't tell somebody like you.

721
00:53:51,145 --> 00:53:52,354
Why?

722
00:53:52,938 --> 00:53:56,150
- What's wrong with me?
- I try to serve life.

723
00:53:57,484 --> 00:53:59,153
But you only...

724
00:53:59,486 --> 00:54:01,447
Seem to want to destroy it.

725
00:54:01,613 --> 00:54:03,282
Ah, father...

726
00:54:04,116 --> 00:54:07,244
You're so wrong. Let me explain.

727
00:54:11,331 --> 00:54:13,333
Life, which you so nobly serve...

728
00:54:13,500 --> 00:54:16,336
Comes from destruction,
disorder and chaos.

729
00:54:16,503 --> 00:54:17,880
Now, take this empty glass.

730
00:54:18,046 --> 00:54:21,008
Here it is, peaceful, serene, boring.

731
00:54:21,175 --> 00:54:22,968
But if it is...

732
00:54:23,886 --> 00:54:25,179
Destroyed...

733
00:54:29,391 --> 00:54:31,769
Look at all these little things.
So busy now.

734
00:54:31,935 --> 00:54:34,271
Notice how each one is useful.

735
00:54:37,191 --> 00:54:41,153
What a lovely ballet ensues,
so full of form and color.

736
00:54:41,320 --> 00:54:44,698
Now, think about all those people
that created them.

737
00:54:44,865 --> 00:54:46,158
Technicians, engineers.

738
00:54:46,325 --> 00:54:49,244
Hundreds of people who will be able
to feed their children tonight...

739
00:54:49,411 --> 00:54:53,290
So those children can grow big and
strong and have children of their own...

740
00:54:53,457 --> 00:54:54,875
And so on and so forth.

741
00:54:55,042 --> 00:54:58,045
Thus adding to the great chain...

742
00:54:58,545 --> 00:54:59,963
Of life.

743
00:55:02,508 --> 00:55:04,092
Female voice: Water. Fruit.

744
00:55:04,259 --> 00:55:07,095
You see, father,
by creating a little destruction...

745
00:55:07,262 --> 00:55:08,347
A cherry.

746
00:55:08,514 --> 00:55:10,307
I'm, in fact, encouraging life.

747
00:55:10,891 --> 00:55:13,727
In reality, you and I are
in the same business.

748
00:55:14,645 --> 00:55:15,687
Cheers.

749
00:55:16,355 --> 00:55:18,649
[♪♪♪]

750
00:55:21,193 --> 00:55:22,694
[Choking]

751
00:55:32,913 --> 00:55:35,040
Where's the robot
to pat you on the back?

752
00:55:36,708 --> 00:55:37,835
Or the engineer?

753
00:55:38,001 --> 00:55:39,837
[Carnival music playing]

754
00:55:43,215 --> 00:55:45,884
Or their children, maybe?

755
00:55:54,935 --> 00:55:58,939
You see now how all your so-called
power counts for absolutely nothing?

756
00:55:59,648 --> 00:56:04,278
How your entire empire of destruction
comes crashing down...

757
00:56:04,444 --> 00:56:08,490
All because of one little cherry.

758
00:56:18,166 --> 00:56:19,334
[Grunting]

759
00:56:21,837 --> 00:56:23,589
You saved my life...

760
00:56:23,755 --> 00:56:26,008
And in return, I'll spare yours...

761
00:56:26,633 --> 00:56:27,968
For now.

762
00:56:28,427 --> 00:56:29,678
You're a monster, Zorg.

763
00:56:31,722 --> 00:56:33,223
I know.

764
00:56:37,227 --> 00:56:39,521
Torture who you have to,
the president, I don't care.

765
00:56:39,688 --> 00:56:41,815
Just bring me those stones.

766
00:56:42,482 --> 00:56:44,067
You have one hour.

767
00:56:44,234 --> 00:56:46,236
[♪♪♪]

768
00:56:51,491 --> 00:56:53,493
[Satellites beeping]

769
00:56:58,999 --> 00:57:01,960
It's gobbling up all the communications
satellites in the galaxy.

770
00:57:02,127 --> 00:57:04,838
Why in the hell is it eating up
all the satellites?

771
00:57:05,005 --> 00:57:06,715
We're working on it, Mr. President.

772
00:57:18,518 --> 00:57:21,021
I've contacted the mondoshawan.
They deplore the incident...

773
00:57:21,188 --> 00:57:22,648
But they accept our apologies.

774
