1257
01:25:39,092 --> 01:25:40,385
Paradise!

1258
01:25:40,552 --> 01:25:41,928
[Electronic music playing]

1259
01:25:42,095 --> 01:25:45,557
Ruby rhod at your service for two hours
with korben and the hotel manager...

1260
01:25:45,724 --> 01:25:48,560
And miss gemini croquette in person...

1261
01:25:48,727 --> 01:25:50,812
And 8000 other lucksters here...

1262
01:25:50,979 --> 01:25:55,817
To enjoy the privilege of the unique
concert of miss plavalaguna!

1263
01:25:55,984 --> 01:25:57,444
[Buzzing]

1264
01:25:59,237 --> 01:26:01,490
And now we enter what must be...

1265
01:26:01,657 --> 01:26:04,326
The most beautiful concert hall
in all the universe!

1266
01:26:04,493 --> 01:26:08,580
A perfect replica
of the old opera house...

1267
01:26:09,081 --> 01:26:10,749
But who cares?

1268
01:26:10,916 --> 01:26:14,503
To my right, a row of ministers,
more sinisters than ministers.

1269
01:26:14,670 --> 01:26:18,215
To my left, baby ray,
star of stage and screen.

1270
01:26:18,382 --> 01:26:21,218
He's not gonna get much out
of this concert, because he's stone-deaf!

1271
01:26:22,094 --> 01:26:23,553
To who?

1272
01:26:24,221 --> 01:26:27,557
And here we have Roy Von baker,
king of laser ball.

1273
01:26:27,724 --> 01:26:31,228
And here, the emperor of kodar japhet
and his lovely daughter.

1274
01:26:31,395 --> 01:26:34,606
"I love to sing,"
she recently confessed to me.

1275
01:26:34,773 --> 01:26:37,275
By the way, I have a recording
of her talented voice.

1276
01:26:37,442 --> 01:26:39,569
[Sound of woman moaning plays]

1277
01:26:39,736 --> 01:26:42,256
I'll play you the rest of the song
after the concert, because right now...

1278
01:26:42,280 --> 01:26:45,117
It's time for korben to say
the word of the day.

1279
01:26:45,742 --> 01:26:50,080
So tell me, my man,
you happy here in the big world?

1280
01:26:54,459 --> 01:26:57,337
And now champagne!

1281
01:27:03,468 --> 01:27:05,804
Commercial! Commercial!

1282
01:27:05,971 --> 01:27:07,639
Man [on earpiece]:
Break for 30 seconds.

1283
01:27:07,806 --> 01:27:09,182
[Buzzing]

1284
01:27:11,518 --> 01:27:12,644
[Sighs]

1285
01:27:18,233 --> 01:27:19,359
[Growling]

1286
01:27:34,458 --> 01:27:36,460
[Classical music playing]

1287
01:27:54,019 --> 01:27:57,022
[Singing inva mulla tchako's
Aria of "Lucia di lammermoor"]

1288
01:29:17,894 --> 01:29:21,565
Commander, I have a ship in trouble
requesting permission to clock for repairs.

1289
01:29:21,731 --> 01:29:23,066
Put him in the docking garage.

1290
01:29:23,233 --> 01:29:24,943
- Inform security.
- Sir.

1291
01:29:25,110 --> 01:29:26,712
Man [on radio]:
Permission granted for one hour.

1292
01:29:26,736 --> 01:29:27,821
More than I need.

1293
01:29:39,958 --> 01:29:41,418
[Knocking on door]

1294
01:29:41,585 --> 01:29:42,919
Yes?

1295
01:29:43,086 --> 01:29:45,088
Man: Champagne for the diva.

1296
01:29:50,468 --> 01:29:51,887
[Gunshot]

1297
01:29:53,013 --> 01:29:54,306
[Gunshot]

1298
01:30:02,147 --> 01:30:03,565
[Speaking in foreign language]

1299
01:30:05,483 --> 01:30:07,319
[Panting]

1300
01:30:21,124 --> 01:30:23,001
I found it.

1301
01:30:44,898 --> 01:30:46,900
[M]

1302
01:30:54,366 --> 01:30:56,159
[Dance music playing]

1303
01:30:57,911 --> 01:30:58,995
Get her!

1304
01:31:05,377 --> 01:31:08,004
[Singing inva mulla tchako's
"the diva dance"]

1305
01:31:08,171 --> 01:31:09,339
Huh?

1306
01:31:24,187 --> 01:31:25,730
[Grunting]

1307
01:31:46,793 --> 01:31:48,253
[Gun clicks]

1308
01:32:11,526 --> 01:32:13,153
[Music ends]

1309
01:32:20,410 --> 01:32:22,412
[All cheering]

1310
01:32:33,131 --> 01:32:34,549
It was an ambush.

1311
01:32:34,716 --> 01:32:36,342
[Growling]

1312
01:32:38,261 --> 01:32:42,432
If it's war they want,
it's war they'll get!

1313
01:32:45,435 --> 01:32:47,312
Bravo! Bravo!

1314
01:32:47,479 --> 01:32:49,606
Bravo! Bravo.

1315
01:32:49,773 --> 01:32:51,399
My compliments, little lady.

1316
01:32:51,566 --> 01:32:55,612
Thank you for doing all the dirty work.
I couldn't have done a betterjob myself.

1317
01:32:56,446 --> 01:32:57,822
Hand over the stones.

1318
01:32:59,783 --> 01:33:00,909
[Gun cocks]

1319
01:33:38,321 --> 01:33:40,490
Nobody move!
We're taking over the ship!

1320
01:33:45,203 --> 01:33:46,704
Hands up!

1321
01:33:48,748 --> 01:33:51,000
[Audience screaming]

1322
01:34:01,177 --> 01:34:03,388
Ruby! Ruby!

1323
01:34:22,574 --> 01:34:23,908
[Screaming]

1324
01:34:41,092 --> 01:34:42,844
[Gunfire]

1325
01:34:43,011 --> 01:34:44,721
[Crowd screaming]

1326
01:34:54,856 --> 01:34:56,441
I know this music.

1327
01:34:58,776 --> 01:35:00,904
Let's change the beat.

1328
01:35:04,741 --> 01:35:06,618
[Ticking]

1329
01:35:07,243 --> 01:35:09,579
Something's happening here.
I think we're being attacked.

1330
01:35:09,746 --> 01:35:11,956
I don't know who they are,
but they're everywhere. Wait.

1331
01:35:12,123 --> 01:35:14,292
I see one of them.
They're warriors, and they're ugly.

1332
01:35:14,459 --> 01:35:17,545
They got big teeth and they got big
foreheads and big ears, and they stink.

1333
01:35:17,712 --> 01:35:18,796
Mangalores.

1334
01:35:18,963 --> 01:35:21,382
[M]

1335
01:35:21,549 --> 01:35:24,052
Korben: The government sent me
to help you. Just stay calm.

1336
01:35:24,219 --> 01:35:28,348
If somebody hears this,
come and get me. I'm in the first row.

1337
01:35:28,514 --> 01:35:30,016
[Growling]

1338
01:35:30,391 --> 01:35:33,102
- You must give her the stones.
- Who?

1339
01:35:33,269 --> 01:35:34,979
The fifth element.

1340
01:35:35,146 --> 01:35:39,317
The supreme being sent to earth
to save the universe.

1341
01:35:39,484 --> 01:35:42,153
- Leeloo?
- Yes.

1342
01:35:43,029 --> 01:35:46,407
But she's more fragile
than she seems.

1343
01:35:46,950 --> 01:35:48,993
She needs your help...

1344
01:35:49,702 --> 01:35:51,663
And your love...

1345
01:35:51,829 --> 01:35:55,416
Or she will die.

1346
01:35:57,043 --> 01:35:59,295
[Groaning]

1347
01:35:59,462 --> 01:36:02,048
- No, no, no. Stay with me.
- Help!

1348
01:36:03,174 --> 01:36:05,301
[Crying]

1349
01:36:09,347 --> 01:36:14,102
If you want something done,
do it yourself. Yep!

1350
01:36:14,269 --> 01:36:17,689
Come on, honey. You can't die.
Come on. Listen to me. Wake up!

1351
01:36:17,855 --> 01:36:19,399
- Where are the stones?
- What?

1352
01:36:19,565 --> 01:36:22,026
The stones. Where are the stones?

1353
01:36:22,193 --> 01:36:23,403
The stones.

1354
01:36:31,202 --> 01:36:33,204
[Laughing]

1355
01:36:35,123 --> 01:36:36,958
[Crying]

1356
01:36:37,125 --> 01:36:39,043
They're not here.

1357
01:36:39,877 --> 01:36:41,879
The stones, where are they?

1358
01:36:43,589 --> 01:36:45,091
In me.

1359
01:36:45,508 --> 01:36:47,343
What? What?

1360
01:36:53,683 --> 01:36:55,893
Oh, my god, korben.
Korben, another one coming.

1361
01:36:56,060 --> 01:36:57,895
Korben. Korben, I think we should go.

1362
01:36:58,062 --> 01:36:59,564
One minute. Just give me a minute.

1363
01:36:59,731 --> 01:37:01,566
Mangalore: Hey, you!

1364
01:37:02,108 --> 01:37:03,818
I said, you.

1365
01:37:03,985 --> 01:37:05,653
- I'm not with him.
- Where's the other?

1366
01:37:06,612 --> 01:37:07,905
[Ruby screams]

1367
01:37:08,072 --> 01:37:09,324
[Gun cocks]

1368
01:37:09,490 --> 01:37:11,090
I said, one minute. Ruby, hold this gun.

1369
01:37:11,242 --> 01:37:13,619
- What? What do you want me to do?
- Hold this gun.

1370
01:37:13,786 --> 01:37:15,580
- Come on. Put your hand on it.
- Oh, my god.

1371
01:37:15,747 --> 01:37:17,540
- Got it? Hold it.
- What do I do?

1372
01:37:17,707 --> 01:37:19,584
If he moves, squeeze the trigger.

1373
01:37:20,585 --> 01:37:22,425
I don't feel right.
I don't feel right, korben.

1374
01:37:22,587 --> 01:37:24,922
The stones are "in me."

1375
01:37:34,599 --> 01:37:36,768
Korben, I got a headache. This ain't me.

1376
01:37:53,034 --> 01:37:54,285
[Gunshot]

1377
01:37:55,453 --> 01:37:57,538
Sorry. Sorry. Sorry.

1378
01:37:57,705 --> 01:37:58,915
Think he's gonna be okay?

1379
01:37:59,916 --> 01:38:02,251
[Growling]

1380
01:38:06,547 --> 01:38:08,925
Oh, my god. Oh, my god, korben.
Another one coming.

1381
01:38:11,511 --> 01:38:13,304
Aw, shit. Three coming, korben. Three.

1382
01:38:14,764 --> 01:38:16,015
[Screams]

1383
01:38:16,182 --> 01:38:18,017
Listen, you guard this with your life...

1384
01:38:18,184 --> 01:38:20,544
Or you're gonna look like
this guy right here. You green?

1385
01:38:20,686 --> 01:38:22,522
-Green. Korben: Super-green?

1386
01:38:22,688 --> 01:38:24,291
- Ruby: Super-green.
- Is that your idea...

1387
01:38:24,315 --> 01:38:25,733
Of a discreet operation?

1388
01:38:25,900 --> 01:38:29,695
Don't worry, sir. I know my man.
He'll calm things down.

1389
01:38:29,862 --> 01:38:31,739
[Gunfire]

1390
01:38:42,166 --> 01:38:43,459
All right.

1391
01:38:49,382 --> 01:38:51,717
[Yelling]

1392
01:38:56,973 --> 01:38:58,599
Move! Move!

1393
01:39:00,226 --> 01:39:01,727
Oh, my god. Oh, my god.

1394
01:39:01,894 --> 01:39:04,647
Ladies and gentlemen.
Ladies and gentlemen, this is amazing.

1395
01:39:06,732 --> 01:39:08,985
- Let me do it.
- Right.

1396
01:39:15,616 --> 01:39:18,870
Oh, my god. Korben Dallas, korben,
my man. Korben Dallas is in trouble.

1397
01:39:21,873 --> 01:39:23,708
Hey. Ray!

1398
01:39:25,710 --> 01:39:26,794
The gun!

1399
01:39:28,671 --> 01:39:30,506
Give me the gun. The gun. The gun!

1400
01:39:30,673 --> 01:39:36,220
I'm gonna go and try to see
if I can see something a little closer.

1401
01:39:52,862 --> 01:39:54,572
Yes, the gun. Yeah.

1402
01:40:03,831 --> 01:40:04,874
Thanks, ray.

1403
01:40:06,000 --> 01:40:09,504
Don't shoot! Don't shoot!
Don't shoot! I'm not armed!

1404
01:40:09,670 --> 01:40:10,713
Gmum

1405
01:40:10,880 --> 01:40:13,341
you've got the wrong guy! Don't shoot!

1406
01:40:13,508 --> 01:40:14,800
I'm not armed! I'm not armed!

1407
01:40:14,967 --> 01:40:16,469
[Growls]

1408
01:40:18,429 --> 01:40:19,514
Oh, my god.

1409
01:40:19,680 --> 01:40:21,015
Korben: I'm on vacation.

1410
01:40:21,182 --> 01:40:25,311
It's... don't shoot me, please.
I'm on a vacation. I won a...

1411
01:40:26,687 --> 01:40:27,813
Contest.

1412
01:40:27,980 --> 01:40:31,526
Gemini croquette's to fhloston paradise.

1413
01:40:34,195 --> 01:40:35,655
Down.

1414
01:40:37,281 --> 01:40:39,367
- Wait a minute. Wait a minute.
- Get down!

1415
01:40:39,534 --> 01:40:41,285
[M]

1416
01:40:41,452 --> 01:40:43,162
I think he's trying
to say something to me.

1417
01:40:43,329 --> 01:40:45,581
- Get down!
- Okay.

1418
01:40:47,792 --> 01:40:49,252
[Screams]

1419
01:40:52,213 --> 01:40:54,215
[Gunfire]

1420
01:40:58,719 --> 01:40:59,845
Sorry. Sorry, my man.

1421
01:41:07,520 --> 01:41:10,481
Korben. Korben?
Where are you, man?

1422
01:41:11,857 --> 01:41:14,485
Oh, my god. Oh, my god. Korben.

1423
01:41:14,652 --> 01:41:16,904
They're coming.
Korben, they're coming.

1424
01:41:17,071 --> 01:41:18,573
[Ruby crying]

1425
01:41:18,739 --> 01:41:20,199
Korben!

1426
01:41:20,950 --> 01:41:22,827
- Don't move.
- What?

1427
01:41:26,622 --> 01:41:29,166
[Screams]

1428
01:41:33,212 --> 01:41:36,048
- What you doing?
- Count to 10.

1429
01:41:43,931 --> 01:41:46,142
- Korben? Was that a bomb?
- Just shut up and count!

1430
01:41:46,309 --> 01:41:49,353
One, two, three, four, five...

1431
01:41:49,520 --> 01:41:51,731
Six, seven, eight...

1432
01:41:52,940 --> 01:41:54,817
Nine...

1433
01:41:58,487 --> 01:42:00,197
[Ruby screaming]

1434
01:42:07,580 --> 01:42:09,707
[Ruby panting]

1435
01:42:09,874 --> 01:42:12,126
[Screams]

1436
01:42:19,884 --> 01:42:21,886
[Ticking]

1437
01:42:25,681 --> 01:42:29,560
I am very disappointed!

1438
01:42:30,227 --> 01:42:32,396
Korben, my man.
Korben, what are you looking for?

1439
01:42:32,563 --> 01:42:33,773
Control room.

1440
01:42:35,608 --> 01:42:37,368
- This is it.
- I'll be over here, all right?

1441
01:42:37,443 --> 01:42:38,944
Let's go! Let's go!

1442
01:42:42,239 --> 01:42:44,241
Quiet! Quiet!

1443
01:42:45,326 --> 01:42:47,662
- You in charge?
- Yeah.

1444
01:42:47,828 --> 01:42:49,580
How many of them are out there?

1445
01:42:50,414 --> 01:42:52,083
- I don't know.
- Let's count.

1446
01:42:52,249 --> 01:42:53,918
[Mangalores growling]

1447
01:42:55,586 --> 01:42:57,630
Seven on the left. Five on the right.

1448
01:43:01,884 --> 01:43:03,594
[Gunfire]

1449
01:43:04,095 --> 01:43:06,055
Four on the right. Two on the left.

1450
01:43:07,473 --> 01:43:10,234
We need to find the leader.
Mangalores won't fight without the leader.

1451
01:43:10,643 --> 01:43:13,020
One more shot
and we start killing hostages.

1452
01:43:14,146 --> 01:43:17,316
- That's the leader.
- Send someone to negotiate.

1453
01:43:19,527 --> 01:43:21,862
[Stammering]
I've never negotiated.

1454
01:43:22,029 --> 01:43:24,031
You mind if I try?

1455
01:43:24,198 --> 01:43:25,950
No, no. Sure, sure. Sure.

1456
01:43:26,117 --> 01:43:28,619
We're sending somebody in
to negotiate!

1457
01:43:32,039 --> 01:43:33,290
[Gunshot]

1458
01:43:37,503 --> 01:43:39,588
Anybody else wanna negotiate?

1459
01:43:39,755 --> 01:43:42,383
Where did he learn
to negotiate like that?

1460
01:43:42,967 --> 01:43:44,260
I wonder.

1461
01:43:48,806 --> 01:43:50,349
Where's Ruby?

1462
01:43:51,142 --> 01:43:52,601
I thought he was dead.

1463
01:43:52,768 --> 01:43:54,061
Master!

1464
01:43:54,478 --> 01:43:57,148
It was nothing, really.
It was just a helping hand.

1465
01:43:57,648 --> 01:44:00,025
Ladies and gentlemen,
this is Ruby rhod...

1466
01:44:00,192 --> 01:44:02,278
Still alive. Aah!

1467
01:44:02,445 --> 01:44:05,030
What's wrong with you? It hurt!

1468
01:44:07,199 --> 01:44:09,201
Wow. Zoom.

1469
01:44:09,368 --> 01:44:10,870
[Cornelius chuckles]

1470
01:44:11,036 --> 01:44:14,832
Korben, I realize
that you must be pretty mad at me...

1471
01:44:14,999 --> 01:44:17,479
But I want you to know
that I am fighting for a noble cause.

1472
01:44:17,626 --> 01:44:20,421
Yes, you're trying to save the world.
I remember.

1473
01:44:20,921 --> 01:44:22,882
Right now I'm trying
to save leeloo, father.

1474
01:44:23,048 --> 01:44:25,843
- Leeloo's in trouble?
- When is leeloo not in trouble?

1475
01:44:26,010 --> 01:44:28,387
- There. Where is that?
- Man: That's the diva's suite.

1476
01:44:29,221 --> 01:44:30,639
Leeloo.

1477
01:44:30,806 --> 01:44:32,516
[M]

1478
01:44:32,683 --> 01:44:34,894
Leeloo. Hang on.

1479
01:44:38,314 --> 01:44:41,567
Here, come on. How the hell do you
get yourself into these positions?

1480
01:44:42,735 --> 01:44:44,028
Come on.

1481
01:44:47,239 --> 01:44:50,242
Yeah, I'm here. It's all right.
It's all right. Everything's okay now.

1482
01:44:50,701 --> 01:44:51,911
Listen.

1483
01:44:52,077 --> 01:44:54,288
[Ticking]

1484
01:44:54,455 --> 01:44:57,374
I got the stones.
All right, just take it easy, all right?

1485
01:44:57,541 --> 01:44:58,834
[Whimpers]

1486
01:45:00,044 --> 01:45:04,006
My man, my man, my man.
What's this thing with all these numbers?

1487
01:45:04,173 --> 01:45:06,175
[M]

1488
01:45:11,889 --> 01:45:13,808
No, no, no.

1489
01:45:13,974 --> 01:45:15,601
Because if it was a bomb...

1490
01:45:15,768 --> 01:45:19,355
The alarms would go off because all
these hotels have bomb detectors. Right?

1491
01:45:19,522 --> 01:45:21,857
[Alarm buzzing]

1492
01:45:22,024 --> 01:45:24,144
Female voice [on loudspeaker]:
This is a type a alert.

1493
01:45:24,193 --> 01:45:27,863
For security reasons,
the hotel must be evacuated.

1494
01:45:29,114 --> 01:45:30,783
Please proceed calmly
to the lifeboats...

1495
01:45:30,950 --> 01:45:32,451
Stay calm!

1496
01:45:32,618 --> 01:45:34,119
Located in the main hallways.

1497
01:45:34,286 --> 01:45:35,496
Please, stay calm!

1498
01:45:35,663 --> 01:45:37,540
[All screaming]

1499
01:45:39,625 --> 01:45:40,668
Stay calm.

1500
01:45:40,835 --> 01:45:43,879
Korben. Korben, my man,
you know how to stop this, right?

1501
01:45:45,923 --> 01:45:47,299
Korben?

1502
01:45:49,510 --> 01:45:53,138
Female voice [on loudspeaker]:
Two minutes to complete evacuation.

1503
01:45:54,807 --> 01:45:57,643
- Get back!
- Evacuation! Evacuation!

1504
01:45:57,810 --> 01:46:01,105
Sorry, sir, you can't stay here.
There's a bomb in the hotel.

1505
01:46:06,110 --> 01:46:07,278
I know.

1506
01:46:09,655 --> 01:46:11,407
[All screaming]

1507
01:46:22,251 --> 01:46:25,045
- Ruby: I don't want to die.
- Please, my son.

1508
01:46:25,629 --> 01:46:26,964
Get in. Get in.

1509
01:46:31,802 --> 01:46:35,222
Female voice [on loudspeaker]:
One minute to total evacuation.

1510
01:46:39,059 --> 01:46:40,311
This one.

1511
01:46:43,814 --> 01:46:46,191
Forty-five seconds.

1512
01:46:48,819 --> 01:46:50,613
Korben: Get her strapped in.

1513
01:46:55,326 --> 01:46:58,203
Korben, korben. Korben, my man,
you know how to fly this thing?

1514
01:46:58,370 --> 01:46:59,580
Just like driving a cab.

1515
01:46:59,997 --> 01:47:01,999
[Engine whirring]

1516
01:47:04,376 --> 01:47:06,170
But the door?
How we gonna get out the door?

1517
01:47:19,683 --> 01:47:22,061
Fifteen seconds.

1518
01:47:26,315 --> 01:47:29,860
Ten, nine, eight...

1519
01:47:30,027 --> 01:47:34,490
Seven, six, five...

1520
01:47:35,741 --> 01:47:37,201
[Exhales]

1521
01:47:38,410 --> 01:47:39,745
[Grunts]

1522
01:47:40,663 --> 01:47:42,122
[Beeping]

1523
01:47:51,340 --> 01:47:53,175
For the honor.

1524
01:47:54,385 --> 01:47:56,053
[Ticking]

1525
01:47:57,179 --> 01:47:58,263
Oh, no.

1526
01:47:59,306 --> 01:48:01,308
- You should hold on.
- Aah!

1527
01:48:13,195 --> 01:48:14,530
Come on.

1528
01:48:19,952 --> 01:48:21,370
[Exhales]

1529
01:48:22,538 --> 01:48:23,747
Like driving a cab.

1530
01:48:25,749 --> 01:48:28,419
Ladies and gentlemen,
it is now 7 P.M. time for the news.

1531
01:48:28,585 --> 01:48:30,754
See you tomorrow
for a new adventure.

1532
01:48:30,921 --> 01:48:32,881
Man [on earpiece]:
End of transmission.

1533
01:48:33,549 --> 01:48:35,551
That's the best show I ever did.

1534
01:48:37,052 --> 01:48:38,178
[Exhales]

1535
01:48:38,345 --> 01:48:41,181
Mr. President, major Dallas has
the five elements on board...

1536
01:48:41,348 --> 01:48:44,268
And the priest is guiding them
directly to the temple.

1537
01:48:45,102 --> 01:48:47,104
[M]

1538
01:48:48,731 --> 01:48:50,024
We're saved.

1539
01:48:51,025 --> 01:48:53,027
[Snoring]

1540
01:49:06,248 --> 01:49:09,126
The diva said
that I should take care of you.

1541
01:49:09,918 --> 01:49:12,546
Humans act so strange.

1542
01:49:12,713 --> 01:49:14,131
What do you mean?

1543
01:49:15,632 --> 01:49:17,634
Everything you create...

1544
01:49:17,801 --> 01:49:19,386
Is used to destroy.

1545
01:49:21,638 --> 01:49:25,309
We call it human nature.
You learn about that on your screen?

1546
01:49:25,476 --> 01:49:28,771
I'm not finished yet. I'm up to v.

1547
01:49:29,146 --> 01:49:30,773
V is good.

1548
01:49:30,939 --> 01:49:32,816
Some very good words in v.

1549
01:49:32,983 --> 01:49:34,443
Like what?

1550
01:49:36,612 --> 01:49:37,946
Valiant.

1551
01:49:38,530 --> 01:49:40,032
Vulnerable.

1552
01:49:42,159 --> 01:49:43,869
Very beautiful.

1553
01:49:49,291 --> 01:49:51,293
[All cheering]

1554
01:49:55,631 --> 01:49:58,133
President: Oh, of course, munro!

1555
01:49:59,468 --> 01:50:01,970
- Mr. President?
- Yes, now what?

1556
01:50:05,307 --> 01:50:06,642
We have a problem.

1557
01:50:12,064 --> 01:50:13,524
What do you mean, it's advancing?

1558
01:50:13,690 --> 01:50:17,361
It's moving at incredible speed.
We're having trouble following it.

1559
01:50:21,824 --> 01:50:25,119
And do you have any idea
where it's heading?

1560
01:50:32,000 --> 01:50:34,878
Korben, there's a general
on the, urn, phone.

1561
01:50:35,712 --> 01:50:37,881
I'll give you to the president.

1562
01:50:38,549 --> 01:50:41,510
Major Dallas, I first would like
to salute a warrior.

1563
01:50:41,677 --> 01:50:43,477
You're a shining example
of this army's might.

1564
01:50:43,637 --> 01:50:45,931
- Mr. President.
- In the name of the federation...

1565
01:50:46,098 --> 01:50:48,142
Any idea when you're
gonna be getting to the point?

1566
01:50:49,143 --> 01:50:50,394
[Sighs]

1567
01:50:50,561 --> 01:50:55,357
Okay. There's a ball of fire 1200 miles
in diameter heading straight for earth...

1568
01:50:55,524 --> 01:50:59,027
And we have no idea how to stop it.
That's the problem.

1569
01:50:59,653 --> 01:51:00,946
[Sighs]

1570
01:51:02,197 --> 01:51:03,657
How much time do we have?

1571
01:51:04,700 --> 01:51:08,162
If its speed remains constant,
in an hour and 57 minutes.

1572
01:51:09,246 --> 01:51:11,248
I'll call you back in two hours.

1573
01:51:11,415 --> 01:51:14,376
Hello? Hello? Hello?

1574
01:51:16,503 --> 01:51:18,505
[M]

1575
01:52:24,696 --> 01:52:26,240
They just landed in the desert.

1576
01:52:28,659 --> 01:52:30,410
Cornelius: Good job, David.

1577
01:52:31,912 --> 01:52:34,206
- Put her in the center.
- Where? Here?

1578
01:52:41,922 --> 01:52:43,674
You got it figured out, father?

1579
01:52:43,840 --> 01:52:46,385
This one should be fire.

1580
01:52:46,551 --> 01:52:48,591
- You know how all this works?
- Theoretically, yes.

1581
01:52:48,679 --> 01:52:52,140
- Theoretically?
- The four stones should go around.

1582
01:52:52,307 --> 01:52:54,351
The fifth element should be
in the middle...

1583
01:52:54,518 --> 01:52:57,646
And then the weapon
against evil should work.

1584
01:52:57,813 --> 01:52:59,573
You've never seen this work before,
have you?

1585
01:53:01,525 --> 01:53:04,945
Every weapon has a manual.
I'm sure this has one too.

1586
01:53:13,495 --> 01:53:16,331
That's it. That's it.
Match up the symbols. Go! Go!

1587
01:53:20,627 --> 01:53:22,671
My man, what you doing?

1588
01:53:22,838 --> 01:53:24,756
- What?
- What you doing?

1589
01:53:25,966 --> 01:53:27,759
Trying to keep you in the dj business.

1590
01:53:31,471 --> 01:53:32,723
Fire.

1591
01:53:34,016 --> 01:53:35,100
Done.

1592
01:53:35,267 --> 01:53:39,104
- So, what happens now?
- So now we have to open them.

1593
01:53:40,230 --> 01:53:43,608
- And you know how to do that, right?
- Theoretically...

1594
01:53:51,283 --> 01:53:54,036
Leeloo, wake up, honey, wake up.
You have to help us.

1595
01:53:54,202 --> 01:53:57,039
Leeloo. How do you open these stones?

1596
01:54:01,752 --> 01:54:03,295
Fire burns.

1597
01:54:03,462 --> 01:54:06,757
Yes, I know all that.
But how do you open these stones?

1598
01:54:07,132 --> 01:54:08,675
Rain...

1599
